From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 62/76] perf(sumcheck): AVX-512 IFMA kernel for the stride-2
 fold

New ecc/fields/ifma_field.hpp: runtime-dispatched (CPUID + BB_FIELD_NO_IFMA kill switch) 8-lane
5x52-bit Montgomery arithmetic in bb's R = 2^256 domain for BN254-sized fields, with AoS <-> limb-major
transposes. fold_stride2 (sumcheck partial evaluation, Gemini fold, translator fold) runs its bulk
through the kernel; the virtual-zero prefix and the tail keep the scalar loop, and blocks of eight
bit-identical pairs are copied like the scalar per-pair short-cut. Exact field arithmetic, so every
output equals the scalar result (computed outputs are fully reduced).
